meta {
  name: List Campaign Records
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/mailer-campaigns/{{campaignId}}/records?q=9c41b2d7ee01
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  q: 9c41b2d7ee01
  ~page: 1
  ~pageSize: 25
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the short printed form resolves to the row", function () {
    // The assertion `controlNumberKeys` exists for: either printed form is one
    // indexed equality, not a substring scan.
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.total).to.equal(1);
    expect(body.items[0].name).to.equal("Dana Okafor");
    expect(body.items[0].controlNumber).to.equal(
      "#7c1e4a90-1111-4b8a-9f10-9c41b2d7ee01",
    );
  });

  test("the row carries its market and its own carrier agency code", function () {
    const row = res.getBody().items[0];
    // 99999 was resolved to Tulsa in the preview, and the run used exactly that.
    expect(row.market).to.equal("Tulsa");
    expect(row.carrierAgencyId).to.equal("A0B9049");
    // `null` = visible to every agency, matching `assignment.mode: 'all'`.
    expect(row.visibleAgencyIds).to.equal(null);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /platform/mailer-campaigns/:campaignId/records — the detail's records table

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `platform:mailers:read`
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`)

  ## Query
  | param | notes |
  |---|---|
  | q | **Any text the table renders** — see below. |
  | page / pageSize | 1-based; pageSize ≤ 100, default 25. |

  ## How `q` is resolved (PAC-101)

  Two things happen, and they are **ORed** — neither suppresses the other.

  **1. The whole term as a control number.** It is normalized by
  `mailerControlNumberKey` (upper-case, non-alphanumerics stripped) and matched
  as one indexed equality against `controlNumberKeys`, which answers **both**
  printed forms — `controlno` (`#` + a UUID) and `New Control Number` (that
  UUID's last 12 hex characters) are different strings on every one of the
  671,339 legacy rows, and legacy fell back to `ENDS_WITH`/`CONTAINS_SUBSTR`, a
  collection scan on every keystroke. This is matched against the *untokenized*
  term on purpose: `#3f2a-91c7` must not be split into two words.

  **2. Tokenized substring match across every rendered column.** The term is
  lower-cased, accent-stripped and split into at most 4 tokens; every token must
  match something, but not all in the same field — so `smith mcalester` finds a
  Smith in Mcalester.

  | Column | Field(s) |
  |---|---|
  | Name | `fullName`, `firstName`, `lastName` |
  | Location | `address.city`, `address.state`, `address.zip` |
  | Market | `market` |
  | Code | `carrierAgencyId` |
  | *(not a column)* | `address.street` |

  Offer (`premium.yearly`) is **not** searched — numeric.

  ### What changed

  The name match used to be **anchored** (`^`) on `firstName`/`lastName` only.
  The Name cell renders `fullName`, so pasting it back into the box asked for a
  first or last name *beginning with* `"Karen Anderson"` — unsatisfiable. And
  because the importer splits a combined name on the first space,
  `MARY ANN SMITH` is stored as `lastName: "ANN SMITH"`, which an anchored match
  could not reach even from the bare surname.

  ### Cost

  `campaignId` stays outside the search, so the scan is bounded by one campaign.
  Measured on a 20,405-row campaign (the real week-29 file size): ~50ms
  execution regardless of token count, with the
  `{campaignId, lastName, firstName}` index still serving the sort. Token count
  is free — `$and` short-circuits per document.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "page": 1, "pageSize": 25, "total": 1, "totalPages": 1,
    "items": [{
      "id": "…",
      "controlNumber": "#7c1e4a90-1111-4b8a-9f10-9c41b2d7ee01",
      "newControlNumber": "9c41b2d7ee01",
      "name": "Dana Okafor", "city": "Bartlesville", "state": "OK",
      "zip": "99999-5807", "market": "Tulsa", "premiumYearly": 1886.15,
      "carrierAgencyId": "A0B9049", "visibleAgencyIds": null
    }]
  }
  ```

  `visibleAgencyIds: null` means every agency, including ones onboarded later.

  ## Errors
  - `401` / `403` — missing token, or missing `platform:mailers:read`.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such campaign.
}
